※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=0 diag=none host=host.c
※ pl4g-test: args -shared

※ **A record laid out for C is answered to C, and by C, as C answers a
※ `struct`.**  `host.c` loads this shared object and calls the functions it
※ offers, each answering one by value, and they in turn call functions of the
※ host's that do the same: the C compiler on the other side is what says
※ whether each member arrived in the register it looked in.
※
※ Sixteen bytes and less are answered in registers -- on x86-64 an eightbyte
※ of whole numbers in `rax` or `rdx` and one of floating-point numbers in
※ `xmm0` or `xmm1`, the two `float`s of one in the one register -- and anything
※ larger through room the caller made, whose address is handed over first and,
※ on x86-64, answered back.  A function the host defines answering one is
※ found the way every host function is, by a stub that keeps every register an
※ argument may be in while it asks: the address of that room among them.

@[abi]
type Pair = whole : i64 ; part : f64

@[abi]
type Floats = x : f32 ; y : f32 ; z : f32

@[abi]
type Quad = a : i64 ; b : f64 ; c : i32 ; d : f64

@[host("host_pair")]
fn host_pair(n: i64) → Pair

@[host("host_floats")]
fn host_floats(x: f32) → Floats

@[host("host_quad")]
fn host_quad(n: i64, x: f64) → Quad

※ What the host calls, each answering a record whole.

@[visible, cdecl]
fn make_pair(n: i64, x: f64) → Pair:
    Pair(.whole ← n, .part ← x)

@[visible, cdecl]
fn make_floats(x: f32) → Floats:
    Floats(.x ← x, .y ← x + 1f32, .z ← x + 2f32)

@[visible, cdecl]
fn make_quad(n: i64, x: f64) → Quad:
    Quad(.a ← n, .b ← x, .c ← 77i32, .d ← x + 0.5f64)

※ And what calls the host's, saying with a number which answer was wrong.

@[visible, cdecl, impure]
fn ask_host() → i64:
    let p: Pair = host_pair(40i64)
    let f: Floats = host_floats(1.5f32)
    let q: Quad = host_quad(50i64, 2.25f64)
    if p.whole ≠ 41i64 ∨ ¬(p.part ≅ 0.75f64):
        1i64
    elif ¬(f.x ≅ 1.5f32) ∨ ¬(f.y ≅ 3f32) ∨ ¬(f.z ≅ 4.5f32):
        2i64
    elif q.a ≠ 51i64 ∨ ¬(q.b ≅ 4.5f64) ∨ q.c ≠ 52i32 ∨ ¬(q.d ≅ 6.75f64):
        3i64
    else:
        0i64
